WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.153 --> 00:00:15.124
In lingering darkness of the dawn, Passepartout had climbed up the funeral pyre from the back, where he

2
00:00:15.184 --> 00:00:15.945
couldn't be seen.

3
00:00:18.107 --> 00:00:23.392
Then, profiting from the billows of smoke, he had braved the flames and saved the woman from death!

4
00:00:24.493 --> 00:00:29.740
Without losing a moment, the four men disappeared into the jungle with Aouda.

5
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.982
They returned to the elephant and, thanks to their skillful guide, escaped quickly.

6
00:00:34.762 --> 00:00:38.184
For the first hour, Passepartout laughed happily at his success.

7
00:00:40.645 --> 00:00:42.626
Sir Francis shook his hand heartily.

8
00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:45.947
Fogg said simply, "Well done!"

9
00:00:46.347 --> 00:00:48.628
which, from him, was high praise, indeed.

10
00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:56.612
Wrapped in a traveling blanket, Aouda rested on Kiouni's back until they reached the train station at Allahabad.

11
00:00:58.464 --> 00:01:01.827
It was ten o'clock, and the journey to Calcutta would take 24 hours.

12
00:01:03.388 --> 00:01:08.152
They would have just enough time to catch the steamer for Hong Kong on October 25 at noon.

13
00:01:09.693 --> 00:01:14.257
Passepartout was sent to purchase some necessities for Aouda, including a dress and a shawl.

14
00:01:15.578 --> 00:01:17.059
While he was away, Mr.

15
00:01:17.099 --> 00:01:20.222
Fogg and Sir Francis helped Aouda to a waiting room in the station.

16
00:01:21.603 --> 00:01:25.586
They watched her anxiously, waiting for her to revive from her long slumber.

17
00:01:26.867 --> 00:01:31.610
She had delicate cheeks, long silken lashes, fine white teeth, and smiling lips.

18
00:01:33.272 --> 00:01:35.473
The men could not help but notice how charming she was.

19
00:01:37.054 --> 00:01:39.956
Passepartout returned a little before the train was about to leave.

20
00:01:41.538 --> 00:01:42.658
Outside the station Mr.

21
00:01:42.698 --> 00:01:45.120
Fogg was paying the guide, who stood with Kiouni.

22
00:01:46.241 --> 00:01:48.222
"You have been a great help," he was saying.

23
00:01:48.242 --> 00:01:52.345
"I have paid you for your service but not for your devotion.

24
00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.567
Would you like to have this elephant?

25
00:01:55.447 --> 00:01:55.948
He is yours."

26
00:01:57.664 --> 00:01:59.105
The guide's eyes glistened.

27
00:01:59.125 --> 00:02:02.387
"You are giving me a fortune!"

28
00:02:02.728 --> 00:02:03.288
he cried.

29
00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:06.510
Mr. Fogg and his friends then boarded the train.

30
00:02:08.111 --> 00:02:12.074
Kiouni trumpeted good-bye, and the guide waved as the train left the station.

31
00:02:13.335 --> 00:02:19.740
Phileas Fogg, Sir Francis Cromarty, Passepartout, and Aouda were soon seated in their car, traveling at full speed.

32
00:02:22.301 --> 00:02:27.994
It took two hours to reach the train's first stop at Benares, and during the journey, Aouda fully

33
00:02:28.054 --> 00:02:29.315
recovered from her drowsiness.

34
00:02:30.596 --> 00:02:36.101
She was astonished to find herself in a car on a train, dressed in European clothing, and surrounded

35
00:02:36.141 --> 00:02:36.862
by strangers.

36
00:02:38.063 --> 00:02:40.766
Her companions immediately told her what had transpired.

37
00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:45.530
With tears in her eyes, she thanked her saviors repeatedly.

38
00:02:48.412 --> 00:02:51.996
She knew, however, that her husband's family would not stop searching for her.

39
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.242
Danger would follow her as long as she remained in India.

40
00:02:57.763 --> 00:03:01.305
When she explained that she had a merchant relative in Hong Kong, Mr.

41
00:03:01.345 --> 00:03:03.167
Fogg offered to escort her there safely.

42
00:03:04.928 --> 00:03:07.370
At half-past 12, the train arrived in Benares.

43
00:03:08.971 --> 00:03:10.712
This was Sir Francis' destination.

44
00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.875
He wished them all success on their journey and said good-bye.

45
00:03:16.236 --> 00:03:19.858
From Benares the train passed through the valley of the Ganges River.

46
00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:26.934
The travelers could see mountains; fields of barley, wheat, and corn; and jungles with green alligators.

47
00:03:28.856 --> 00:03:33.578
They passed villages at the edges of thick forests and elephants bathing in sacred rivers.

48
00:03:36.139 --> 00:03:38.541
Night fell and the train continued at full speed.

49
00:03:40.162 --> 00:03:45.485
In the dark the passengers heard the roars of tigers, bears, and wolves, which fled at the sound

50
00:03:45.505 --> 00:03:46.285
of the locomotive.

51
00:03:47.946 --> 00:03:50.968
The train reached Calcutta at seven in the morning on October 25.

52
00:03:52.756 --> 00:03:53.456
According to Mr.

53
00:03:53.476 --> 00:03:56.697
Fogg's journal, that was the exact date scheduled for his arrival.

54
00:03:58.158 --> 00:04:00.178
He was neither behind nor ahead of time.

55
00:04:02.199 --> 00:04:06.600
The two days he had gained between London and Bombay had been lost in the journey across India.

56
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.901
But Phileas Fogg did not regret the loss in the least!

57
00:04:11.402 --> 00:04:14.703
The train entered the station, and Passepartout jumped out first.

58
00:04:15.083 --> 00:04:19.344
Mr. Fogg followed and held out his arm to help his fair companion down from the train.

59
00:04:20.884 --> 00:04:25.807
Mr. Fogg intended to proceed at once to the Hong Kong steamer so that Aouda could get comfortably

60
00:04:25.847 --> 00:04:26.727
settled for the voyage.

61
00:04:27.948 --> 00:04:31.250
He was unwilling to leave her side while she remained on dangerous ground.

62
00:04:32.251 --> 00:04:35.312
Just as they were leaving the station, a policeman approached Mr.

63
00:04:35.352 --> 00:04:36.913
Fogg and said, "Mr.

64
00:04:37.214 --> 00:04:38.274
Phileas Fogg?"

65
00:04:38.294 --> 00:04:41.116
"I am he," replied Fogg.

66
00:04:41.136 --> 00:04:43.117
"Is this your servant?"

67
00:04:43.537 --> 00:04:45.838
asked the policeman, pointing to Passepartout.

68
00:04:45.858 --> 00:04:47.860
"Yes," said Mr.

69
00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:53.108
Fogg. "Both of you, be good enough to follow me," commanded the policeman.

70
00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:56.712
Mr. Fogg betrayed no surprise or alarm.

71
00:04:58.233 --> 00:05:03.038
Passepartout tried to explain that they had no minutes to spare, but the policeman tapped him with his

72
00:05:03.098 --> 00:05:04.079
stick, and Mr.

73
00:05:04.119 --> 00:05:06.221
Fogg gave Passepartout a signal to obey.

74
00:05:06.241 --> 00:05:08.724
"May this young lady come with us?"

75
00:05:09.204 --> 00:05:09.785
asked Mr.

76
00:05:09.805 --> 00:05:12.948
Fogg. "She may," replied the policeman.

77
00:05:14.632 --> 00:05:20.376
Mr. Fogg, Aouda, and Passepartout were conducted to a four- wheeled carriage drawn by two horses.

78
00:05:21.997 --> 00:05:25.219
They took their seats next to the policeman and were soon on their way.

79
00:05:26.841 --> 00:05:32.625
During the twenty-minutes that elapsed between leaving the train station and arriving at the courthouse, no one spoke.

80
00:05:37.548 --> 00:05:41.030
As our train traveled to Calcutta, we saw the famous Ganges River.

81
00:05:41.931 --> 00:05:43.132
I must say, it was beautiful.

82
00:05:44.396 --> 00:05:48.820
The river runs a little more than 1,500 miles, from the Himalayas all the way to the Bay

83
00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:52.764
of Bengal, through some of the most fertile and populated land in the world.

84
00:05:54.286 --> 00:05:57.509
According to Hinduism, the Ganges River is the holiest of rivers.

85
00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:03.094
Its water is considered holy, and Hindus believe that bathing in it will wash away sin.

86
00:06:03.875 --> 00:06:08.599
As a result many Indians travel great distances every year to drink and bathe in the river's holy

87
00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:14.657
water. It is also believed that spreading one's ashes in the river after death leads to quicker salvation.
